<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Beshbaliq</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Beiting, Bishbalik</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Beshbaliq, 'five towns', was a city in the north of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tian-shan">Tian Shan</a>, near modern Jimsar in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xinjiang">Xinjiang</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang dynasty</a> it was the seat of the Beiting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">Protectorate</a>, and from the 9th century it served as the summer capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uyghurs">Uyghur</a> kingdom of Qocho. It remained an important centre under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a>, when it was a base of the Chagatai realm, and its ruins survive.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/beshbaliq.jpg" alt="Beshbaliq" width="320" height="243" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Croquant · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Location_of_Jimsar_within_Xinjiang_(China).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
